  "source_excerpts": {
    "title": "Subresultant pivot strata for exact Semaev elimination",
    "mechanism": "Object: a guarded subresultant decision tree with complete exceptional branches. Operation set Sigma: test a principal subresultant coefficient, select the valid remainder recurrence, or descend to its zero stratum. Trichotomy: branching; this is a solver/representation object, not a lossy quotient under the full group translation action. Discarded information: many tuples share a pivot pattern; the pivot pattern alone is not a solution and branch formulas retain coordinate recovery. Eliminate each internal S_3 chain variable by subresultants rather than materializing a single large resultant. Guard each division by its principal coefficient, and carry equations for its vanishing branch. This can exploit common generic pivot sequences while representing degree drops exactly. Polynomial degree at output and degree used to certify the guards are separately measured.",
    "minimal_test": {
      "design": "p=101,211,431; m=2,3,4; generic and j=0,1728 panels labeled separately. Enumerate base tuples and compare all signed group sums against all retained branches.",
      "execution_status": "design_only_not_approved",
      "controls": [
        {
          "kind": "baseline",
          "design": "One unrestricted branch retaining the complete resultant and all exceptional tests equals the direct elimination baseline."
        },
        {
          "kind": "matched_null",
          "design": "Random coefficient chains with matching multidegrees and graph."
        },
        {
          "kind": "known_false",
          "design": "Force the leading coefficient to zero while a genuine solution remains; the unguarded recurrence must fail and the guarded tree must recover it."
        },
        {
          "kind": "identity",
          "design": "Use the stated baseline slice with identical inputs, ordering and certificate policy; output identities must match exactly."
        },
        {
          "kind": "generic_group",
          "design": "For any claimed group information gain, repeat the statistic on relabelled Z/NZ with the same incidence and acquisition budget. Algebra-only comparisons explicitly do not claim a generic-group escape."
        }
      ],
      "required_metrics": [
        "number of pivot strata K, max coefficient degree, exceptional mass, coefficient operations",
        "all setup, acquisition, unsuccessful-attempt, transport, certificate and verification costs",
        "peak resident memory and total stored bytes",
        "SAT and UNSAT costs separately, or successful and failed incidence attempts separately",
        "loss L=log2(number of represented preimages) and branching b=max verified successors at each retained synopsis; witness storage separately"
      ],
      "budget": {
        "proposed_only": true,
        "maximum_runs": 0,
        "note": "This handoff approves zero runs. A successor needs a new frozen per-cell budget; planning allowance 3 implementation-days and up to 4 CPU-hours/32 GiB for first complete toy cell, scaled only by Coordinator approval. Exhaustive synthetic calibrators may warrant smaller documented bounds."
      },
      "stopping_rules": [
        "Stop on first soundness/completeness control failure and classify the instrument invalid.",
        "At a frozen resource cap report failed_infrastructure without a mathematical verdict.",
        "If valid completed cells miss the quantitative threshold, reject only this mechanism/parameter claim and retain the measured obstruction."
      ],
      "required_artifacts": [
        "frozen source formula/curve/base and seeds",
        "all candidate descriptions and failed attempts",
        "exact control and solution certificates",
        "stage-cost and memory records",
        "independent checker source binding",
        "unpooled raw metrics"
      ]
    },
    "falsification_conditions": [
      "Any valid completed cell exhibits the known-false failure: Force the leading coefficient to zero while a genuine solution remains; the unguarded recurrence must fail and the guarded tree must recover it.",
      "The completed controlled ladder fails the proposed effect: Total operations <=0.5 resultant baseline with zero root-set mismatches; K grows slower than the product of elimination degrees on the toy arity ladder",
      "The charged saving disappears after including construction, canonicalization, failed attempts, memory or recovery.",
      "A purported synopsis merges the collision pair without retaining its distinction: Same resultant degree and same generic root count but different degree-drop branches cannot be conflated."
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Public generated mathematical instances only, with frozen field, subgroup, curve, factor-base definition, presentation, solver and sample law.",
      "F2 factor-base decomposition is a component, not the proposed new object; the added object is a guarded subresultant decision tree with complete exceptional branches. F1 generic search is a comparator; any F7 caching/preprocessing is fully charged.",
      "All identity, soundness and completeness certificates must be independently checked before measuring cost.",
      "Prime-field digit/implicit membership is a high-degree or implicit-description escape class of KN-OPEN-020, not a bounded-degree plane-locus exemption. Binary arms use actual Weil descent and never transfer Boolean identities to F_p."
    ],
    "proof_search_map": {
      "bottleneck": "The exact load-bearing step is producing and using a guarded subresultant decision tree with complete exceptional branches cheaply enough for: Total operations <=0.5 resultant baseline with zero root-set mismatches; K grows slower than the product of elimination degrees on the toy arity ladder",
