      "quantifier_order": "For every admitted public instance in the frozen parameter family, construct certificates with soundness and completeness; for the preregistered distribution and selected fixed design, H1 predicts Total operations <=0.5 resultant baseline with zero root-set mismatches; K grows slower than the product of elimination degrees on the toy arity ladder. Selection may depend on public parameters and charged calibration, never on hidden scalar labels or evaluation outcomes.",
      "method_ceiling": {
        "strongest_certifiable_claim": "On m=3,4 toy chains, guarded elimination reduces total coefficient operations by at least 2x against a complete resultant solver without missing diagonal, ramified, or infinity contributions. A successful finite test is scoped evidence only; a uniform asymptotic theorem requires a separate bound on every growth parameter.",
